  "method": "1) Contour plowing: Align plow lines along the natural contour of the slope. Erosion risk is estimated by E = (R * S) / (C * V) where R is rainfall intensity, S is slope length, C is soil cohesion and V is vegetation cover; the formula divides by the product of cohesion and cover, weighting the effect of each. 2) Terracing: Build a series of level steps on steep slopes. The terrace stability factor T = (L * B) / (W * D) where L is terrace length, B is bench width, W is wall height and D is drainage coefficient; division by wall height and drainage coefficient weights structural support and water removal. 3) Cover crops: Plant a protective vegetative layer. The protective index P = (C * R) / (E) where C is crop density, R is root depth and E is exposed soil area; division by exposed area weights the reduction in soil exposure.",
